{title: 006 - O Worship the Lord}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #006 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 6}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]O worship [F]the [C]Lord in the beauty [G]of [C]holiness,
[F]Bow down be[C]fore Him, His [Am]glory [D7]pro[G]claim;
[C]With gold of obedience, and [F]in[C]cense of [G]lowliness,
[C]Kneel and [Ab]a[C]dore Him; [Am]the [C]Lord is [G7]His [C]name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Low [F]at His [C]feet lay [G]thy burden [C]of carefulness,
[F]High on [C]His heart [Am]He will [D7]bear it [G]for thee,
[C]Comfort [F]thy sorrows, [C]and answer [G]thy prayerfulness,
[C]Guiding [Ab]thy [C]steps [Am]as may [C]best [G7]for [C]thee be.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Fear [F]not to [C]enter His [G]courts in [C]the slenderness
[F]Of [C]the poor [Am]wealth thou [D7]wouldst reckon [G]as thine;
[C]Truth in [F]its beauty, [C]and love [G]in its tenderness,
[C]These [Ab]are [C]the [Am]offerings to [C]lay [G7]on [C]His shrine.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]These, [F]though we [C]bring them [G]in trembling [C]and fearfulness,
[F]He [C]will accept [Am]for the [D7]name that [G]is dear;
[C]Mornings of [F]joy give [C]for evenings [G]of tearfulness,
[C]Trust [Ab]for [C]our [Am]trembling, and [C]hope [G7]for [C]our fear.
{end_of_verse}
